    "about": {
      "hero": {
        "heading": "About Flexbrace",
        "text": "Developed by a licensed orthotist / CPO Certified Prosthetist Orthotist with over 50 years of experience in orthotic technology. Flexbrace® has helped users since 2001."
      },
      "who": {
        "heading": "Who we are",
        "p1": "We are Flexbrace – a company focused on drop foot orthoses. Behind the product is Lars Falkenman, licensed orthotist / CPO Certified Prosthetist Orthotist with over 50 years of experience in orthotic technology (since 1975). Flexbrace® has helped users since 2001: a light, discreet and individually fitted brace for anyone who needs better foot lift and more confident walking.",
        "p2": "Our focus is simple: more freedom of movement, less risk of tripping, and a brace you can live with every day."
      },
      "history": {
        "heading": "Our history",
        "p1": "The story begins in the summer of 1975, when Lars worked in an orthotics department in Borås. Even then he saw how often drop foot orthoses were used – and how inadequate they were. They were bulky, limited in function and far from user-friendly.",
        "p2": "That sparked a lifelong ambition: to create an orthosis that was lighter, more discreet and, above all, more functional.",
        "p3": "As a licensed orthotist / CPO Certified Prosthetist Orthotist, Lars continued working in orthotics departments in Borås and Gothenburg, served as head of orthotics at Linköping University Hospital, and worked internationally in Brussels (CEBELOR) and Copenhagen (Nyrop & Maag). Over the years he kept developing drop foot orthoses – but without the major breakthrough.",
        "p4": "The breakthrough came in 2001. A patient, Gerner Hemmingsen, had suffered a serious cerebral blood clot with hemiplegia. Everyday life became difficult and undignified – including when he could not get up from the floor on his own. That made a strong impression.",
        "p5": "After 26 years of experience, Lars decided: now or never. Almost every orthosis on the market had been tried without satisfactory results. Something entirely new was needed.",
        "p6": "In September 2001 the first prototype was ready. It was named Flexbrace®. When Gerner received his new orthosis he walked across the kitchen floor without difficulty, turned around and said: “I should have had this five years ago.” In that moment Flexbrace® was born.",
        "p7": "To document the effect, 50 prototypes were made for different user types. After two months users could choose: continue with Flexbrace® or return to their previous orthosis. In an early evaluation with 50 users, all chose to continue with Flexbrace®. Patent work then began, and interest grew quickly in media and among clinics.",
        "p8": "Flexbrace® is used today at Center for Hjerneskade in Copenhagen, among others, and has been featured on the Danish TV programme Lægens Bord."
      },
      "vision_mission_heading": "Vision & mission",
      "vision_label": "Vision:",
      "vision": "That more people with drop foot can walk with greater confidence, more naturally and with greater dignity in everyday life.",
      "mission_label": "Mission:",
      "mission": "To offer a light, discreet and functional drop foot orthosis – developed from real patient needs – where support, comfort and individual fitting go hand in hand.",
      "what": {
        "heading": "What we do",
        "p1": "We make Flexbrace® available to anyone who needs support for drop foot: an ankle-foot orthosis that lifts the forefoot, stabilises the ankle and supports a more natural gait. The product is developed in Europe, manufactured in Italy, and designed to fit in regular shoes.",
        "p2": "We work with clear product information, the right fit and a path from need to solution – so more people get access to the difference Lars once saw was missing on the market."
      },
      "values": {
        "heading": "Our values",
        "1": "Function before prestige – the brace should make a difference in real steps, not just on paper",
        "2": "Discretion and dignity – assistive devices should show as little as possible and feel as good as possible",
        "3": "The individual at the centre – drop foot looks different for everyone; the solution should follow the need",
        "4": "Experience and honesty – over 50 years of orthotic practice behind every decision",
        "5": "Quality in the details – from design to manufacturing"
      },
      "team": {
        "heading": "The team",
        "lars_name": "Lars Falkenman",
        "lars_bio": "Licensed orthotist / CPO Certified Prosthetist Orthotist and inventor of Flexbrace®. Former head of orthotics at Linköping University Hospital; has worked in Borås, Gothenburg, Brussels and Copenhagen. With over 50 years of experience in orthotic technology, Lars shaped the product around what he missed in care: a brace that is both effective and possible to live with. Flexbrace® has helped users since 2001.",
        "note": "[Feel free to add Oscar, Anton, Glenn and others with short roles here when you want to show the Swedish team.]"
      },
      "competence": {
        "heading": "Our expertise",
        "1": "Deep specialist expertise in drop foot and ankle-foot orthoses (AFO)",
        "2": "Over 50 years of orthotic experience from Sweden and abroad",
        "3": "Product development from idea and prototype to patented solution (Flexbrace® since 2001)",
        "4": "Individual fitting with a focus on gait function, balance and comfort",
        "5": "European development and manufacturing in Italy"
      }
    },
    "product": {
      "tabs": {
        "label": "Product information",
        "overview": "Overview",
        "specs": "Specifications",
        "delivery": "Delivery",
        "faq": "FAQ",
        "about": "About Flexbrace"
      },
      "overview": {
        "heading": "Product overview",
        "intro": "Flexbrace® is a light and discreet drop foot orthosis (ankle-foot orthosis) designed for anyone who has difficulty lifting the foot while walking. When foot lift fails, the risk increases that the toes catch on the ground, that gait becomes uneven and that balance is affected. Flexbrace® provides controlled lift of the forefoot, stabilises the ankle and supports a more natural gait pattern.",
        "body": "The product is developed in Europe by a licensed orthotist / CPO Certified Prosthetist Orthotist with over 50 years of experience in orthotic technology. Flexbrace® has helped users since 2001. That makes Flexbrace® unique: a compliant brace without unnecessary stiffness, with enough support to lift and stabilise – and a feel that makes it easier to wear for longer periods in everyday life.",
        "does": {
          "heading": "What Flexbrace® does",
          "intro": "Drop foot often means reduced ability to lift the forefoot (dorsiflexion). That can make people lift the leg higher than normal, stumble more easily and compensate with the whole body. Flexbrace® helps to:",
          "1": "lift the foot in the swing phase",
          "2": "stabilise the ankle",
          "3": "improve gait toward a more natural movement",
          "4": "increase balance and confidence in every step",
          "5": "reduce the risk of toes catching on the ground"
        },
        "design": {
          "heading": "Design and comfort",
          "intro": "Flexbrace® is built to show as little as possible and feel as light as possible:",
          "1": "Low weight – about 100 grams",
          "2": "Discreet fit that often works in regular shoes",
          "3": "High comfort for daily use",
          "4": "Compliant construction that supports without unnecessarily “locking” the foot",
          "closing": "The goal is a brace you actually want to wear – not just one that works in theory."
        },
        "manufacturing": {
          "heading": "Manufacturing",
